 function guide(stage){const sections=[
  ['1. Import a companion',['Open Model and choose New companion.','Enter a name and choose Male or Female.','Use a self-contained GLB with a skeleton and clips named idle, talk, walk, sit, sit-enter, sit-exit. Export an uncompressed model under 15 MB.','If the model exceeds 15 MB, choose a downsizer quality and tap Downsize to 15 MB; this reduces textures, not geometry or animations. Download the processed GLB if needed.','If it is not rigged, expand Add a skeleton, choose a clean A- or T-pose and forward direction, then tap Add humanoid skeleton. Inspect the approximate rig in Preview model in 3D or Blender. Use Meshy or Blender for difficult meshes and prepare the required animations separately.','Preview model in 3D, then Start poser. Drag teal joints; drag empty space to orbit. Reset pose or download joint rotations as a JSON file. These are preview poses, not new animation clips.','Save Companion. The new character is available in your local developer VR gallery. Existing game companions can be edited without importing their models again.']],
  ['2. Give them a personality',['Choose the companion, then Personality.','Describe them and adjust the sliders.','Choose a dialogue category and type one spoken line per row.','Alternatively, expand Paste ChatGPT personality JSON, copy the prompt into ChatGPT, paste its JSON reply, and press Apply pasted personality.','Save Companion. Their dialogue pools and behavior are used in the local VR room; this is not a live ChatGPT chat service.']],
  ['3. Import voice lines',['Save the words in Personality first.','Open Voice lines, find the line, generate the recording in your chosen voice tool and download it.','Select the MP3, WAV or Ogg recording next to that exact line. A successful import overrides the recorded game line in your draft.','If the words change, import a matching recording again.']],
  ['4. Add a motion',['Choose Animations and Show character in 3D. In Animation templates, select a category and an available clip. Change playback speed and looping as needed.','To create your own motion, start the poser, set the first pose at 0 seconds and capture it. Drag joints to a different pose and capture the next keyframe at a later time. Play custom animation to interpolate rotations. Download or load template JSON; for your own imported companion GLB, export the custom animation GLB to import below. This is not AI inbetweening.','To generate a motion with AI, write a short movement description and copy it to Meshy Text to Motion. Generation is external, subject to the provider’s policy and credits.','For FBX or BVH, use Blender to retarget the clip onto a compatible skeleton and export a self-contained animated GLB.','Choose the GLB, select the clip inside it, name it, and save it to your local animation library.','Select a target model and preview. The editor rejects incompatible skeletons and rest poses. Testing another NPC does not modify its shipped animation list.','To test it in the VR room, preview it on the selected companion, then add it to that companion. Open the VR room and choose the motion in their interaction menu.']],
  ['5. Create a mission giver',['Select an existing game companion and open Mission giver.','Create a mission giver draft using their model, name, short role and any imported voice recordings. A new local-only model must be integrated into the game build first.','The NPC Editor opens. Use its map to place them, choose their route and schedule, and give them a mission.','Their VR personality remains separate from their mission dialogue. Use the existing Lines & voice editor to write or reuse lines.','Check and play the mission draft. Publishing is a separate explicit action in the Mission Editor.']],
  ['6. What is local and what is live?',['Imported models, local animation files and companion edits stay on this developer computer. They are not uploaded by Companion Studio.','Use the NPC Editor’s existing Add animation panel for compatible shipped library clips on world NPCs. New local clips need asset integration and catalog validation before publication.','Do not send purchased or No AI licensed assets to external AI services. No automatic API calls, expenses or production deployment occur in this studio.']],
  ['7. Edit on your phone, test on PC',['Open the separate Companion Studio at /vr-companion-studio.html and sign in with your authorized developer Google account. The game itself stays PC-only.','Create or edit a companion and save your work.','Choose Transfer between phone and PC, then Download companion transfer. It includes the saved personality, edited lines, imported model, assigned motions and imported audio.','Move the .vrcompanion file to your PC using your own file-sharing method. In the in-game Companion Studio, open Transfer between phone and PC and import that file.','Choose the companion in the VR gallery to test it, or create a mission giver draft. Signing into the same account does not automatically sync local files.']]];
  for(const [title,steps] of sections){const d=el('details');d.className='companion-guide';d.append(el('summary',title));const list=el('ol');for(const step of steps)list.append(el('li',step));d.append(list);stage.append(d);}}
